Z||000000||Ayrow||11-27-2001||09:09 PM||||Ok, so here I am getting back into the Fiero thing only to discover that many of you guys are doing/have done that which I was told by several body shops, could not be done successfully - That is, painting the Fiero.<P>What's going on now??<BR>Has ten years passed and they now know how to paint the different types of plastics on the Fiero and actually make it durable?<P>I remember back in 1991, when I got my first Fiero, I called all over town looking for somebody that would paint my car.<BR>They all told me that it could not be done "successfully" because of all of the different types of plastics involved - at least not cheaply.<P>Is this still an issue?<P>I was most impressed with FieroLisa's site - she went and did it herself!!!<P>Any opinions on this subject would be most welcome.<P>Thanks,<P>Ayrow<BR>||||reg||5
